[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Queen's Gambit Accepted"]
[Variation "Queen's Gambit Accepted, 3.e4 e5"]
[ECO "D20"]
[Character "sharp,tactical"]
[Risk "medium"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "central-break"]

1. d4 d5 2. c4 dxc4 3. e4 e5 { Counter-strikes at d4. White cannot hold both d4 and c4. }
4. Nf3 exd4 { Wins a second pawn. } 5. Bxc4 Nc6 { Develops and defends d4, so Black keeps the extra pawn for now. }
6. O-O Be6 { Offers to trade the bishop on c4, White's most active piece. }
7. Bxe6 fxe6 { Retakes toward the centre and opens the f-file for the rook. }
8. Qb3 ( 8. Qxd4? { Takes the pawn but loses the queen to the knight. } 8... Nxd4 9. Nxd4 Qxd4 ) 8... Qd7 { Guards e6, which the queen was attacking. }
9. Qxb7 Rb8 { Attacks the queen, which must leave, so Black gains time. } 10. Qa6 Nf6 { Develops. The pawn on d4 cramps White and Black's pieces are more active. } *
